   "explain": "pent-1-ene: CH₂=CHCH₂CH₂CH₃."
  }
 ],
 "takeaways": [
  "**-ene** means one C=C double bond; the **number** says where it starts.",
  "A double bond is **two lines**; the two carbons in it each need only two more bonds.",
  "Check: H atoms = 2 × C for an alkene."
 ],
 "notes": [
  {
   "title": "Exam tip",
   "text": "Always state where the double bond is, both in the name (the number) and in the drawing (two lines between the right pair of carbons)."
  }
 ]
}